<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Listen on IPv4, explicitly.

  The image ships docker_related_config.xml, which sets <listen_host>::</listen_host>
  together with <listen_try>1</listen_try>. On a host without IPv6 every bind then
  fails with "Address family for hostname not supported", listen_try swallows the
  error, and the server comes up listening on nothing at all — alive, logging
  normally, and refusing every connection. The healthcheck fails for the full two
  minutes and takes Metabase down with it, because Metabase waits on a healthy
  warehouse.

  Docker Desktop's VM has IPv6, so this never appears on a laptop. It appears the
  first time the stack runs on a plain IPv4 VPC, which is most of them.

  replace="replace" rather than adding a second entry: the merge would otherwise
  keep the unusable :: alongside this one, and the failure would stay in the log
  looking like the cause of something.
-->
<clickhouse>
    <listen_host replace="replace">0.0.0.0</listen_host>
    <listen_try>1</listen_try>
</clickhouse>
